    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1167-a2">

                <pb facs="1053" n="739" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg739"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>

                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-20T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 20, 1914, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department is informed by Ambassador at London that he has received following
                    telegram from you.</p>
                <p>Please inform British Government that I advise them to allow no Germans to leave
                    England or any British Dominions until I obtain leave British subjects to leave
                    Germany.</p>
                <p>Department is of the opinion that such an exchange of communications should not
                    be made through the good offices of the United States.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                </p>
            </div>
